========================================
PART 4 — GET THE DATA READY (your 9 Parquet files in R2)
========================================

Steps 9 and 10 first (keys). Everything below is already filled in: copy and run.
The folder, file names, text column and id column are found automatically.

---

11. See Your Files in R2

RUN

python scripts\corpus.py r2-list

OUTPUT

    0.278 GiB  training data/....parquet
    ...
9 file(s), 2.5 GiB in r2://ored-datasets/

---

12. Look Inside a File

RUN

python scripts\corpus.py r2-inspect

It opens the first file and downloads only its schema (about 1 MB).

OUTPUT

"file_format": "parquet",
"parquet_schema": [ "id: string", "text: string", ... ]

---

13. Download the Files

RUN

python scripts\corpus.py r2-fetch

All 9 files go to data\raw\training-data (about 3 GB). Files already there are
skipped.

---

14. Train the Tokenizer (once)

RUN

python scripts\corpus.py train-tokenizer

It finds the text column, learns 16,384 tokens from a 300 MB sample of all files
and writes data\tokenizers\ored-bpe-16k-v1.json.

OUTPUT (start)

text column: text | id column: id

OUTPUT (end)

"vocab_size": 16384,

---

15. Build the Training Shards

RUN

python scripts\corpus.py build-shards

It uses all CPU cores but one and writes data\tokens\training-data\v1.
99% of the documents are for training, 1% for validation.
If it stops, run it again: it continues where it stopped.

OUTPUT (end)

"content_sha256": "<64 letters>",
"counts": { "documents": {...}, "tokens": {"train": ..., "val": ..., "test": 0} }

---

16. Upload the Shards to R2

RUN

python scripts\corpus.py publish --dir data\tokens\training-data\v1 --name training-data --version v1

---

17. Register the Dataset in Supabase

RUN

python scripts\corpus.py register --name training-data --version-label v1 --bucket ored-datasets --storage-path "training data" --dataset-type pretraining_corpus

---

18. When You Add or Delete Files

Use v2 (then v3, ...) for the new set of files:

RUN

python scripts\corpus.py r2-fetch --out data\raw\training-data-v2
python scripts\corpus.py build-shards --input data\raw\training-data-v2 --version v2 --reuse-from data\tokens\training-data\v1
python scripts\corpus.py publish --dir data\tokens\training-data\v2 --name training-data --version v2
python scripts\pretrain.py --config configs\ored50m.yaml --set data.tokens.manifest=data\tokens\training-data\v2 --set data.tokens.dataset_version=v2 --init-from checkpoints\ored50m\best.pt --run-name ored50m-v2 --set checkpoint.r2_upload=true

Only the new files are tokenized. Training continues from the old best.pt.

---

========================================
PART 5 — TRAIN
========================================

19. Measure What Fits on the GPU

RUN

python scripts\pretrain.py --probe-batch-size

OUTPUT

{"batch_size": 4, "fits": true, ...}
{"batch_size": 6, "fits": false, ...}

Default: batch 4 x 8 accumulation steps. If 8 fits with room to spare, add
--set data.batch_size=8 --set training.grad_accum_steps=4 to step 20.

---

20. Train (40 epochs)

RUN

python scripts\pretrain.py --set checkpoint.r2_upload=true

It trains ored50m on data\tokens\training-data\v1 for 40 epochs. Every 1000 steps
it checks the validation loss; when it is better, best.pt is replaced in
checkpoints\ored50m\ and in R2 (ored-checkpoints bucket).

OUTPUT (start)

PRETRAINING RUN: ored50m (ored50m)
parameters    : 49,894,912
precision     : bf16
dataset       : training-data v1 (content ...)

It stops early after 5 checks in a row without improvement. To run all 40:

python scripts\pretrain.py --set checkpoint.r2_upload=true --set training.early_stopping_patience=0

For 20 epochs instead:

python scripts\pretrain.py --set checkpoint.r2_upload=true --set training.epochs=20

---

21. Continue Stopped Training

RUN

python scripts\pretrain.py --set checkpoint.r2_upload=true --resume

---

22. If It Runs Out of GPU Memory

RUN

python scripts\pretrain.py --set checkpoint.r2_upload=true --set data.batch_size=2 --set training.grad_accum_steps=16

best.pt is never damaged by a crash.

